    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97547" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγγρᾰφ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who collects and writes down historic facts,
			historian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				7.2.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Th.</u>
				5
			</span></i>: then, generally, <i>prose-writer</i>, opp. poet, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				235c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				278e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				15.35
			</span></i>; and, simply, <i>writer, author</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1150
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				272b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.68K.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.593
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγγραφῆς, οἱ</span>, <i>commissioners appointed to draw up
				measures</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.22.3
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				7.58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>party to a contract</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				636.23
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>.</div>
